#====================================================================
# E999 draft - aarch64 char is unsigned: EOF sentinel comparison fails
# Proposed document: drafts/E999-draft-aarch64-unsigned-char-eof-sentinel.md
#
# 格式规则:
#   - key: value（冒号后一个空格，value 到行尾）
#   - 多行值: 下一行以空格开头 = 续行
#   - 列表值: 逗号分隔
#   - 正则值: | 分隔多个模式
#   - 以 # 开头的行为注释
#====================================================================

id:                     E3525
trigger_tool:           clang|gcc|make
phase:                  runtime
error_signature:        result of comparison of constant -1 with expression of type 'char' is always true|comparison is always true due to limited range of data type|process hangs while reading a file|no output for minutes during file parsing

severity:               3
category:               platform, char-signedness, runtime-hang
match_keywords:         unsigned char, char signedness, fgetc, getc, EOF, -1, always true, aarch64, arm64, infinite loop, hang, tautological-constant-out-of-range-compare
title:                  Keep fgetc/getc results in an int: on aarch64 char is unsigned, so an EOF sentinel never matches and the read loop spins forever

root_cause:             aarch64 has unsigned plain char by default (x86 is signed). Code that stores fgetc()/getc() in a char and compares it against EOF (-1) compiles to a comparison that can never be true, because the stored value is truncated to 0..255. When a read loop relies on that sentinel to stop - typically a "skip to end of line" loop after a buffer-length-limited read - the loop spins at end of file instead of terminating. clang reports it at compile time as -Wtautological-constant-out-of-range-compare.
affected_scope:         Any pre-C++11 era C/C++ source that reads bytes through char. Manifests only when the sentinel is actually reached: a truncated last line, a file whose last line has no trailing newline, or a read that exactly fills the caller buffer. Typical shape: fgets(s, size, f) returns a chunk without '\n', then a skip loop runs to the next newline and reaches EOF.
verification_cmd:       grep -rn --include=*.c --include=*.cpp --include=*.h --include=*.hpp -E '(char|int8_t)[[:space:]]+[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*(fgetc|getc|gzgetc)[[:space:]]*\(' . ; printf 'a' > /tmp/nonl.txt ; printf 'x\n' | cat - /tmp/nonl.txt > /tmp/probe.txt

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           widen-the-sentinel-variable
rec_description:        Keep the byte in an int (or compare before narrowing) so the EOF sentinel survives. The type change is local and has no semantic effect on the byte value itself; also cast the seeding expression from char to unsigned char so the initial value is not sign extended.
rec_command:            sed -i -E 's/for[[:space:]]*\\(char[[:space:]]+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)[[:space:]]*=/for (int \\1 = (unsigned char) /' <file>   # then review each site by hand
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      bounded-skip-loop
fallback_description:   When the declaration cannot be changed (e.g. an ABI-visible struct field), bound the loop by an explicit hit-counter or by feof() so it can never spin even if the sentinel comparison is wrong.
fallback_command:       Add "if (++guard > MAX_LINE_SKIP) break;" inside the skip loop, or test feof(handle) as a second exit condition.
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       .*-fsigned-char.*|.*-funsigned-char.*|.*-Wno-tautological-constant-out-of-range-compare.*|.*#define[[:space:]]+EOF[[:space:]]
forbid_1_reason:        Flipping the global char signedness changes every other char in the program (including string and table handling) and only trades one class of bug for another; silencing the diagnostic or redefining EOF removes the compile-time signal that found the bug in the first place.
forbid_1_consequence:   The same truncation bug survives in other files, and the diagnostic that pinpoints it is gone, so it has to be rediscovered at runtime. In the plast 2.3.2 case the affected build had already emitted the warning and it was not acted on.

principles:             P005, P007, P013
doc_file:               drafts/E999-draft-aarch64-unsigned-char-eof-sentinel.md
last_updated:           2026-10-15
source_event:           plast 2.3.2 on HarmonyOS aarch64: testFastaOutputFrame never returned (12 min CPU) reading sapiens_1Mo.fa; root cause CommonOsImpl.hpp:80

